const v17ReadA={id:"v17-read-a",kind:"passage",label:"Passage for Items 69-72",title:"To the Graduating Class",description:"Graduates, families, and teachers: good morning.\n\nI was asked to give you advice, and I have been told it should be short, because the program is long and the gymnasium is warm. So I will give you only three things.\n\nFirst, learn to be a beginner again. You have spent years becoming good at being a student. Next month many of you will be the newest and least experienced person in a workplace. Ask questions early, while asking still seems natural.\n\nSecond, keep the friends who tell you the truth. Praise is pleasant, but it teaches you very little. The friend who says your plan has a problem is giving you something worth more than a compliment.\n\nThird, remember who carried you here. Somewhere in this room is a parent who skipped a meal so that you could pay a school fee, a teacher who stayed late, a classmate who explained what you missed. You did not get here alone, and you will not get anywhere that matters alone.\n\nThat is all. The rest you will learn the way the rest of us did: slowly, and mostly by making mistakes. Congratulations.",alt:"Short graduation speech giving three pieces of advice: be a beginner again, keep friends who tell the truth, and remember the people who helped you."};
const v17ReadB={id:"v17-read-b",kind:"passage",label:"Babasahin para sa Aytem 73-76",title:"Ang Lumang Radyo",description:"Sa ibabaw ng aparador ni Lolo Pedring ay may lumang radyong de-baterya, kulay kape at may basag na pihitan. Tuwing alas-sais ng umaga, binubuksan niya ito para sa balita at sa ulat ng panahon, kahit may cellphone na ang lahat sa bahay.\n\n'Lolo, nasa cellphone na po lahat iyan,' sabi ni Ben isang umaga, habang inaayos ang antena para sa kanya.\n\n'Alam ko,' sagot ng matanda. 'Pero kapag nawalan ng kuryente at signal, ano ang gagana?'\n\nNatawa si Ben. Hindi pa raw nangyayari iyon.\n\nMakalipas ang dalawang buwan, dumating ang malakas na bagyo. Nawalan ng kuryente ang buong bayan, at pagsapit ng ikalawang araw, patay na ang lahat ng cellphone at wala nang signal. Sa dilim ng sala, ang tanging naririnig ay ang mahinang boses mula sa lumang radyo: ang ulat kung saan bukas ang evacuation center at kung kailan aabot ang tubig sa ilog.\n\nNang matapos ang bagyo, bumili si Ben ng dalawang bagong baterya. Inilagay niya ang mga ito sa tabi ng radyo, nang walang sinasabi.",alt:"Maikling kuwento tungkol sa lumang radyong de-baterya ng isang lolo na naging tanging mapagkukunan ng balita noong bagyo."};
const v17ReadC={id:"v17-read-c",kind:"passage",label:"Passage for Items 77-80",title:"The Last Trip",description:"It was nearly ten at night when Mang Dado pulled his jeepney into the terminal for the last trip. The route was long, the fare small, and on most nights he would have waited until the seats were full. Tonight only three passengers climbed in: a nurse still in her uniform, a boy carrying a box of school projects, and an old woman with a bag of vegetables.\n\n'Aren't you waiting for more?' the nurse asked.\n\nDado looked at the empty benches, then at the boy, who was yawning. 'Not tonight,' he said, and started the engine.\n\nThe road was dark beyond the town proper. When the old woman asked to be dropped at a corner far from any light, Dado did not drive away at once. He kept his headlights on the path until she reached her gate and waved.\n\nAt the end of the route, he counted the coins in the box beside the wheel. It was not enough to cover the diesel. His wife would ask about it in the morning, and he would tell her the truth: that he had made a bad business decision, and that he would probably make it again.",alt:"Short story about a jeepney driver who leaves on his last trip with only three passengers, lights an old woman's way home, and loses money on the trip."};
